> That's indeed a bit odd. It seems that the conversion tooth-crysknife
> deliberately or accidentally drops the 'proofed' bit.

Deliberately. Since crysknives aren't burnable (or any other stripe of
erosionprone), it wouldn't make sense for them to stay fireproof.
(Worm teeth _can_ be burnt; try dipping one into a lit potion of oil,
for example. Hence, fireproofing.)

Fixing, as Simon notes, is Something Else that happens to share a flag
in the code (and hence in the wishing interface), but there's no reason
for one to carry over to the other.

